      "id": 1,
      "text": "Walker Mill takes its name from a historic gristmill that once powered the local African American community in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/maryland_walker-mill",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community was founded in the early 20th century as a planned neighborhood for African American families during segregation, echoing the Great Migration.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/maryland_walker-mill",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Walker Mill Regional Park offers sports fields and walking trails, giving residents a green space for recreation and community gatherings.",
